@startuml E03-infinite-onward-chain
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam nodeBackgroundColor #FFCCBC
skinparam nodeBorderColor #E64A19

title E-03 — Infinite Onward Chain\nServiceRequest.replaces allows unlimited depth; no termination condition

frame "Hop 1 — Facility A (full)" #FFF9C4 {
  node "SR/ref-001\nstatus=active" as sr1
  node "Task/t-001\nstatus=rejected\nbStatus=#referred-onward\nstatusReason=#capacity-full" as t1
}

frame "Hop 2 — Facility B (full)" #FFE0CC {
  node "SR/ref-002\nstatus=active\nreplaces=SR/ref-001" as sr2
  node "Task/t-002\nstatus=rejected\nbStatus=#referred-onward\nstatusReason=#capacity-full" as t2
}

frame "Hop 3 — Facility C (full)" #FFD5A8 {
  node "SR/ref-003\nstatus=active\nreplaces=SR/ref-002" as sr3
  node "Task/t-003\nstatus=rejected\nbStatus=#referred-onward\nstatusReason=#capacity-full" as t3
}

node "..." as dots #FFCCCC

frame "Hop N — Facility N" #FFCCCC {
  node "SR/ref-00N\nstatus=active\nreplaces=SR/ref-00(N-1)" as srN
  node "Task/t-00N\nstatus=???\n(accepted? rejected again?)" as tN #FFAAAA
}

sr1 --> t1 : Task tracks SR
sr1 <-- sr2 : replaces
sr2 --> t2
sr2 <-- sr3 : replaces
sr3 --> t3
sr3 <-- dots
dots <-- srN : replaces
srN --> tN

note right of dots
  All are valid ERefServiceRequests.
  No profile constraint limits chain depth.
  ServiceRequest.replaces is 0..* MS.

  After 10 hops:
  • 10 open ServiceRequests (all status=active)
  • 10 open Tasks (all status=rejected)
  • Patient has been passed to 10 facilities
  • No facility has taken ownership
  • Patient status: unknown
end note

note bottom
  Open queries across all hops:
    GET ServiceRequest?status=active → 10 results (all are this patient's referral chain)
    GET Task?status=rejected         → 10 results (all are this patient's referral chain)

  No FHIR query can efficiently find "the latest unresolved referral for this patient"
  without traversing the full replaces chain — O(N) queries for an N-hop chain.

  The IG does not define:
    • Maximum chain depth
    • Responsibility for breaking a cycle (all-full scenario)
    • What happens when no facility can accept
    • How the patient is notified of failure to find a receiving facility
    • How the original referral is marked as "failed to place"
end note

@enduml
